  "notes": [
    "Exploratory before measurements precede the point-access, tuple/index, numeric-wire and word-comparison optimizations; durability and earlier SQLite insert optimizations were already present.",
    "Early before workloads overlapped CPU profiling and are excluded here; selected late cases ran after that profile. Before and after were separate processes on the same machine, with three warmups and nine samples.",
    "Collection before measurement was isolated before the unchanged-index optimization. Wall-clock values remain sensitive to JIT, GC and machine load.",
    "After report includes bounded work-count probes outside timings and full final-row verification. Before report predates the additional identity/fork probes and full final-row verification.",
    "Browser first/reloaded reports use real WebKit storage. Emulated IndexedDB cases in the after report measure adapter CPU/correctness, not browser IO latency.",
    "CPU sampling covers process setup and final verification as well as the three-second timed worker loop; percentages are diagnostic, not isolated steady-state measurements."
